## Pitfalls hit this round (documented for A-15.1+ subagents)
1. FLAT MIRROR: build source = D:\q4e_build\src (flat layout, CMAKE_HOME_DIRECTORY). The repo subtree is NOT the build source. Sync = copy changed files flat (engine/common/X -> D:\q4e_build\src\common/X), verify with git hash-object.
2. Copy-Item PRESERVES source mtime -> ninja sees file as unchanged -> silent no-op build. After syncing, touch the file (set LastWriteTime) before rebuilding.
3. STALE DEPS: after a header change (common.h), ninja's dependency graph in this build tree was stale and only rebuilt the directly-listed TUs -> mixed old/new common_params layout in llama-common.lib -> 0xC0000005 AV in BOTH exes at startup (zero output). Fix: `cmake --build ... --clean-first` (full rebuild, 477 steps) -> green. RULE: after ANY shared header change, build with --clean-first; do not trust incremental builds in this tree.
4. A killed build mid-CUDA-compile can leave corrupt .cu.obj (LNK1123 "convert to COFF failed"). If link fails with that, delete the affected CMakeFiles dir's .obj files and rebuild.
